// The music program's menu on the Type 340. It holds the screen, the
// light pen, READ TAPE, PLAY and PUNCH, each converter's volume slider,
// the device's room and onset, and the orchestra block a punched tape
// carries (Implementation.md, "Reading a tape").
//
// Included by dacmusic.am1 in bank 0, before its constants. Uses its
// loader and player (lds, ld0, rdb, fp, ct, npart, pbl, ppt, orch, ostp,
// ovol, opl, oroom, onst, per, pla, mnu, NCONV, ORCHN, ORCHCT, ORCHN2,
// ORCHCT2, ORCHN3, SETCFG, NRM, NON), the drum's library as it reads it
// (drd, vld, dir, ninst, vdk, xs), the lists in menus.ac (lsto, lfe,
// aus), PUNCH and the places' tables in punch.ac (pun, plv, pnt), the
// volume with the dynamic in force (dzv, in bank 3), vld's answer 6's
// text (sft, in bank 1), dacdefs.ah's dye and dyo,
// TYPE340/type340defs.ah and LIGHTPEN/lightpen.ah.
//
// An instrument field is a voice of the drum's library, shown by its
// name in the directory (dir, in bank 1). The directory is read again at
// the start, when an instrument's list opens and at READ TAPE, so a
// library written while the menu runs is seen; PLAY loads the voices
// (vld), saying LOADING VOICES meanwhile, or says why it cannot.
//
// The screen is a display list in core, drawn again each time the 340
// stops. Its first words are a gate (mgt), a jump to the menu's body or
// to an open list (menus.ac). The body's texts and the sliders come
// first, then a jump (msw) to the menu's tail, the buttons and the status
// line, ending in a stop. While the piece plays, msw jumps to the play
// tail instead, PLAYING, a STOP target, and a jump back to the list's
// start, so the 340 runs the play screen on its own and the player only
// looks for a hit (phit). Each field the pen can change is drawn with the
// pen on, and is the opener of its list. The fields are a converter's
// place in the stereo field (its row's label), part, instrument and
// octave, the parts a movement, and the device's room and onset under
// the rows. READ TAPE, PLAY and PUNCH are drawn with the pen on too, and
// act at once. The only other points drawn with the pen on are the
// sliders' tracks, so a hit is an opener's or a button's, told by the
// band and column it falls in (fnd), or a track's, which drc gives
// exactly. A hit acts once. The pen must leave them for about 0.14 s
// before the next hit counts, since a pen held still need not hit in
// every frame. The fields are words of the list that fill patches, a
// character word for a number, or a save to the text of a place, a part,
// an instrument or an octave, which returns at the text's end character.
// Display subroutines reach banks 0-1 only, so every text is in bank 0
// or 1. While the piece plays, the openers are drawn with the pen off
// (mpo), so a hit there cannot pause the play screen.
//
// A slider is a row of VN points at the right of its converter's row, the
// rightmost 0 dB and each to its left VSTEP more attenuation, with a
// marker above the point of the converter's level (ovol) and the level in
// whole dB under the track's right end (vmk sets both; the play screen
// draws them too, being the same list). A hit does not simply set its
// point. The hits on one track in a frame are a run, judged with the next
// frame's (vend; Implementation.md, "The menu"). A new level goes to the
// converter at once (dzg), which slews to it without a click; while a
// piece plays, the dynamic in force there is added (dzv).
//
// The menu polls (dsp, dss) and uses no sequence breaks, as the player.

// The point words before text at (px, py), or before a save word (ATS).
#define AT(px, py) next(point); y(py) next(point); x(px) next(character)
#define ATS(px, py) next(point); y(py) next(point); x(px) next(subroutine)
// An opener's or a button's text at (px, py), in mode m (character, or
// subroutine for a save). The pen is turned on first, in an opener's
// word that mpo patches. ATQ, a save word's point words, turns it off
// again.
#define OPN(px, py, m) lpon next(point); y(py) next(point); x(px) next(m)
#define ATQ(px, py) lpoff next(point); y(py) next(point); x(px) next(subroutine)
#define OPON (lpon | next(point)) // an opener's first word, on the menu
#define OPOFF (lpoff | next(point)) // and while the piece plays
#define NOPN 0d17               // the openers, mow's words
// A target at (px, py), STOP's on the play screen. An 18-unit square at
// scale 1, then its point with the pen on, then the pen off again.
#define TGT(px, py) next(point); y((py) - 0d9) next(point); x((px) - 0d9) next(vector); \
    visible right deltax(0d9); visible up deltay(0d9); visible left deltax(0d9); \
    visible down deltay(0d9) end; \
    intensity(7) lpon next(point); y(py) next(point); x(px) show next(parameter); \
    intensity(5) lpoff
// A target's point as drc reports it, x and y each without its low bit.
#define TP(px, py) ((((px) >> 1) << 0d9) | ((py) >> 1))
#define SAVEC (save | next(character))
// The play tail's wait, an invisible vector continued to the raster's
// edge, across the whole screen at scale 0, for two fetches.
#define WAIT next(vcontinue); right deltax(1)
// The pen's aperture, half again APERTURE250's 28. It takes a hit within
// 20 units, short of half the 60 between rows.
#define PENAP 0d42
// The openers and buttons, as fnd numbers them. Each converter's part
// (0-3), instrument (4-7) and octave (8-11), the parts a movement (12),
// READ TAPE (13), PLAY (14), PUNCH (15), each converter's place (16-19),
// the room (20), the onset (24). A number's low two bits are its
// converter, the rest its list's kind.
#define NTGT 0d25
#define NOCT (onam - octbl)     // the octaves, octbl's words
#define AWAYN 0d4000            // passes of the wait without a hit, 0.14 s
#define AWAY (0777777 - AWAYN)  // -4000, for a pool word; law i AWAYN in bank 0 needs none
// fnd's bands and columns, in the screen's units; drc's points are even,
// and every threshold odd. The parts a movement has its band from FPB up.
// The rows' bands are FRP each, down from FRT to FRB (their texts at 780,
// 720, 660 and 600). In a row, the place's opener (n CENTER, 60-172) is
// left of FXV, the part's (PART NONE, 216-342) left of FXP, the
// instrument's (386-624) left of FXI, the octave's (656-726) left of
// FXO, the track from VX0. The buttons' band is FBB to FBT (texts at
// 480). READ TAPE (60-186) is left of FXR, PLAY (260-316) of FXL, PUNCH
// (400-470) of FXU, ROOM BUSCH HALL (560-770) of FXM, ONSET 16 MS
// (820-974) right of it.
#define FPB 0d869
#define FRT 0d817
#define FRP 0d60
#define FRB 0d577
#define FXV 0d195
#define FXP 0d365
#define FXI 0d641
#define FXO 0d745
#define FBT 0d517
#define FBB 0d457
#define FXR 0d223
#define FXL 0d363
#define FXU 0d543
#define FXM 0d795
// The sliders, VN points VDX apart from x VX0. VDX is 1 << 4, VSH its
// shift, VSHD the shift as drc gives x, without its low bit. The levels
// are vlv's, VSTEP (1/8 dB) apart.
#define VN 0d16
#define VX0 0d760
#define VDX 0d16
#define VSH 4s
#define VSHD 3s
#define VSTEP 0d24
// The player's idle turns in about a frame of the play screen. A run of
// hits there ends when this many pass without one.
#define VIDLE 0d64
// RUNLOG builds (a diagnostic) log the runs vend judged, the last 16 of
// them, 6 words each, in the ring rlg (RLOGW words).
#define RLOGW 0d96
// A track's point after the first, the pen on again, since drs turns it
// off.
#define VPT(i) lpon next(point); x(VX0 + (i) * VDX) show next(parameter)
// A slider at height py. Its track, then the move to its marker's point,
// 10 units above, which the marker's word (x, patched) follows.
#define TRACK(py) intensity(5) lpon next(point); y(py) next(point); \
    x(VX0) show next(parameter); \
    VPT(0d1); VPT(0d2); VPT(0d3); VPT(0d4); VPT(0d5); VPT(0d6); VPT(0d7); \
    VPT(0d8); VPT(0d9); VPT(0d10); VPT(0d11); VPT(0d12); VPT(0d13); VPT(0d14); \
    VPT(0d15); \
    intensity(6) lpoff next(point); y((py) + 0d10) next(point)
// The marker, a stroke 10 units up from the point its word moves to.
#define MARK visible up deltay(5) end
// The readout, the level in whole dB, three characters RDY under the
// track, ending under its 0 dB point; the pen stays off. Its words are an
// upper shift, so a text before it cannot leave it in set 2; the text,
// vdb's word for the level, which vmk patches; and the end.
#define RDX 0d958
#define RDY 0d30
#define RDW(a, b, c) (((a) << 0d12) | ((b) << 6) | (c))
#define CSP 040                 // space
#define CMI 055                 // minus
#define CQU 077                 // ?
#define CUP 035                 // upper shift
#define CEND 037                // end
#define CD(d) (060 + (d))       // a digit
#define READOUT(py) intensity(5) next(point); y((py) - RDY) next(point); \
    x(RDX) next(character); RDW(CUP, CUP, CUP)
#define RDE RDW(CEND, CEND, CEND)

// The field words fill patches, in orch's order, and after each
// instrument field the count of its further stops (ostp).
mfw, mpf1; mif1; mof1; mpf2; mif2; mof2; mpf3; mif3; mof3; mpf4; mif4; mof4
mcf, mic1; mic2; mic3; mic4
mlw, mlf1; mlf2; mlf3; mlf4     // each converter's place

// The openers' first words, which mpo patches.
mow, mo1; mo2; mo3; mo4; mo5; mo6; mo7; mo8; mo9; mo10; mo11; mo12; mo13
    mo14; mo15; mo16; mo17

// menu -- the menu, until PLAY, READ TAPE or PUNCH. The program starts
// here, from the console; READ TAPE, PUNCH and the piece's end come back
// to mnr, keeping their status line. Every word the menu reads is set
// here or by the routine that uses it. Memory keeps its words from a run
// that was stopped, and a restart does not reload them. While a list is
// open (lon), a hit is kept for the frame's end, where menus.ac's lfe
// acts on it; a list stays open until it is closed by its OK, DONE,
// CANCEL or header.
// Has no arguments and does not return. It ends at PLAY, READ TAPE or
// PUNCH.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, at menu (from beg) or at mnr.
menu,
    local mn0, mn1, mn2, mn3, mn4, mn5, mn6, mn8
    eem
    law sbl
    jda sts
    dzm rps                 // core outlives a restart of the emulator, its reader's read does not
    dzm xs
    dzm i [aus:1]           // no audition sounding
#ifdef RUNLOG
    law rlg
    dac rlp
    dzm rln
    dzm rfc
#endif
    crossBankjsp(drd:1, NOEEM) // the drum's library
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp mnr
    law snv
    jda sts
mnr,                        // READ TAPE, PUNCH and the piece's end come back here
    eem
    dzm atm
    dzm vro
    dzm hro
    lac mswm                // the list ends in the menu's tail
    dac msw
    lac [OPON]              // the openers drawn with the pen on
    jda mpo
    lac [jump mbody]        // no list open
    dac mgt
    dzm lon
    law PENAP
    dac pap
    dzm arm                 // a pen already on an opener waits until it leaves
    law i AWAYN
    dac qt
    jsp fill
mn0,
    // The aperture is set each frame, since the configuration's overrides
    // one set at start.
    lio pap
    dpy-i LIGHTPEN
    dzm hit
    lio [mlist]
    dla
mn1,
    dsp
    jmp mn2
    drc
    lac lon
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp mn6
    jsp fnd
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [NTGT]
    jmp mn5
    // The frame's first hit is the one that counts.
    add [1]
    dac mt
    law i AWAYN             // the pen is on an opener or a button, so it has not left
    dac qt
    lac hit
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    lac mt
    dac hit
    jmp mn3
    // Neither, so a slider's point, which leaves the arming alone.
mn5,
    jsp vhit
    jmp mn3
    // A list is open. The frame's first hit is kept for lfe, and every
    // hit holds off the arming.
mn6,
    lac hit
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    dio lhw
    law 1
    dac hit
    law i AWAYN
    dac qt
mn3,
    drs
mn2,
    dss
    jmp mn4
#ifdef RUNLOG
    idx rfc
#endif
    jsp vend                // the frame's run ends; with none, the held run is dropped
    lac lon
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp mn8
    lac hit
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp mn0
    lac arm
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp mn0
    dzm arm
    lac hit
    jda act
    jsp fill
    jmp mn0
mn8,
    crossBankjsp(lfe:1, NOEEM) // the list's frame end
    lac lon
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jsp fill                // it closed; the fields as it left them
    jmp mn0
// The wait for the stop counts the pen's absence, about 35 us a pass.
// Each AWAYN passes without a hit arm the next.
mn4,
    isp qt                  // skip when the pen has been away long enough
    jmp mn1
    law 1
    dac arm
    law i AWAYN
    dac qt
    jmp mn1
    endlocal

// act -- act on an armed hit on an opener or a button. An opener's list
// opens (menus.ac's lsto) and act returns; READ TAPE, PLAY and PUNCH do
// not return.
// Takes the opener or button in AC, fnd's number + 1 (1 to NTGT).
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jda.
act, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local acx, ac1, ac2
    dap acx
    lac act
    sub [1]
    dac ltg
    sub [0d13]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp ac1
ac2,
    crossBankjsp(lsto:1, NOEEM)
acx, jmp .
ac1,
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp rdt
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [1]
    jmp mpl
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [2]
    jmp i [pun:3]           // in bank 3 (punch.ac), the window open
    jmp ac2                 // a place's opener
    endlocal

// mpo -- set the openers' first words (mow) to AC, OPON on the menu,
// OPOFF while the piece plays.
// Takes the word in AC.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jda.
mpo, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local mo0, mox, mop
    dap mox
    law mow
    dac mop
    law i NOPN
    dac mpn
mo0,
    lac i mop
    dac mt
    lac mpo
    dac i mt
    idx mop
    isp mpn
    jmp mo0
mox, jmp .

mop, 0                      // mow's next word
    endlocal

// mpl -- PLAY. Load the orchestra's voices from the drum (vld), the menu
// kept drawn with LOADING VOICES; if they cannot be, say why on the
// status line and go back to the menu. Then start the play screen, which
// the 340 runs on its own, and play the piece; its end, or STOP (pso),
// comes back to the menu. The status line is blanked, so a piece that
// ends does not show an earlier STOPPED. The 340 has stopped at the
// menu's frame end, and is let stop there again after the load. With hpl
// set, it halts at lpl first, the voices loaded and the 340 still
// stopped, and at lpe (dacmusic.am1) when the piece is over, so a timing
// taken between the two halts counts the piece alone.
// Has no arguments and does not return. It runs on into pla, or ends at
// mnr.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, from act.
mpl,
    local mp1, mp2, mp3
    law sld
    jda sts
    law 1
    dac mnu
    dac xs
    crossBankjsp(vld:1, NOEEM)
    dzm xs
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp mp1
mp2,
    dsp                     // a pen hit is passed over
    jmp mp3
    drs
mp3,
    dss                     // until the 340 stops at the frame's end
    jmp mp2
    law sbl
    jda sts
    lac hpl
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
lpl, hlt                    // Continue plays
#ifndef NOSCREEN
    lac [OPOFF]             // NOSCREEN builds leave the 340 stopped
    jda mpo
    lac mswp
    dac msw
    lio [PENAP]
    dpy-i LIGHTPEN
    lio [mlist]
    dla
#endif
    jmp pla
    // The voices not loaded; say why.
mp1,
    jda rsn
    jda sts
    jmp mnr
    endlocal

// rsn -- the text saying why vld did not load (svt, by its AC 1-6), a
// damaged voice's number put in its text first.
// Takes vld's answer, 1-6, in AC and returns the text's address in AC.
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jda, from bank 0 or 1. It returns through the full address
// jda leaves, so menus.ac calls it too (crossBankjda).
rsn, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local rs1, rs2, rsr
    dac rsr
    lac vdk
    jda num                 // its digits and the end, which becomes a space
    dac mt
    and [077]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [037]
    jmp rs1
    lac mt
    add [1]
    jmp rs2
rs1,
    lac mt                  // one digit; the end and the code after it become spaces
    add [0140]              // 037 0 becomes 040 040, two spaces
rs2,
    dac sdn
    lac rsn
    add [svt - 1]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    jmp i rsr

rsr, 0                      // the return, a full address
    endlocal

// pso -- STOP, a hit on the play screen. The converters are halted at
// once, the 340 started again, and the menu shown, with STOPPED.
// Has no arguments and does not return. It ends at mnr.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, from phit in the player's main loop.
pso,
    dxh1
    dxh2
    dxh3
    dxh4
    drs
    law sst
    jda sts
    jmp mnr

// phit -- the play screen's pen, from the player's turns with nothing to
// decode. A hit on STOP's point stops the piece (pso); one on a track's
// goes to vhit, and the 340 goes on. The play screen has no frame end the
// program sees, so a run of hits on a track also ends when VIDLE turns
// pass without a hit, and the run vend then holds is dropped when VIDLE
// more pass.
// Has no arguments and no return values. On STOP it does not return.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jsp.
phit,
    local ph1, ph2, phx
    dap phx
    dsp
    jmp ph1
    drc
    dio mt
    lac mt
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [TP(0d240, 0d426)]
    jmp pso
    jsp vhit
    drs
    jmp phx
ph1,
    lac vro
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp ph2                 // no run to end
    isp vq
    jmp phx
    jsp vend
    jmp phx
ph2,
    lac hro
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp phx                 // none held either
    isp vq
    jmp phx
    dzm hro
phx, jmp .
    endlocal

// vhit -- a hit on a track's point, from drc. Extend the run of hits on
// its track, or end the run (vend) and start one. The hits of a frame
// on one track come left to right, so a hit on another track, or at or
// left of the run's last, is a new run. A word that is no track's point
// is passed over. Built with FIRSTHIT, each hit sets its point at once.
// Takes drc's word in IO.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jsp.
vhit,
    local vh1, vh2, vh3, vhx, vw, vx, vy
    dap vhx
    dio vw
    // The track, from y without its low bit, one of vty's.
    lac vw
    and [0777]
    dac mt2
    law vty
    dac mlt
    law NCONV
    dac mln
    lac mt2
    jda look
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [NCONV]
    jmp vhx
    dac vy
    // The point i, from x without its low bit, VX0/2 + i VDX/2.
    lac vw
    rar 9s
    and [0777]
    sub [VX0 >> 1]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp vhx
    sar VSHD
    dac vx
    sub [VN]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp vhx
    law i VIDLE
    dac vq
#ifdef FIRSTHIT
    lac vy
    add [1]
    dac vro
    lac vx
    dac vlo
    dac vhi
    jsp vend
#else
    lac vro
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp vh2                 // no run, so one starts
    sub [1]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME vy
    jmp vh1                 // another track's
    lac vx
    sub vhi
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO_OR_NEGATIVE
    jmp vh3                 // right of the run's last, so the run goes on
vh1,
    jsp vend
vh2,
    lac vy
    add [1]
    dac vro
    lac vx
    dac vlo
vh3,
    lac vx
    dac vhi
#endif
vhx, jmp .

vw, 0                       // drc's word
vx, 0                       // the point, 0 to VN-1 from the left
vy, 0                       // the track, 0 to NCONV-1
    endlocal

// vend -- the run of hits on a track ends. It is held, and judged only
// together with the run before it, if that one was held on the same
// track. A pen put down or lifted partway through a frame gives a run
// cut short, which is then never judged alone. The converter's level is
// kept if its point lies within the two runs' span, else it moves to the
// span's nearer end, into ovol, the marker and the converter (dzg). A
// level that is not one of vlv's (set from the console) lies right of
// every span, so it moves. With no run (a frame with no hit on a track),
// the held run is dropped. Built with FIRSTHIT, a run is judged alone at
// once.
// Has no arguments and no return values.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jsp.
vend,
#ifdef FIRSTHIT
    local ve1, ve2, ve3, ve6, vex, vl, vr, vp, vlu, vhu
#else
    local ve1, ve2, ve3, ve4, ve5, ve6, ve7, vex, vl, vr, vp, vlu, vhu, vht
#endif
    dap vex
    lac vro
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp ve6                 // no run, so the held one is dropped
    sub [1]
    dac vr
#ifdef RUNLOG
    dac rlt
#endif
    add [ovol]
    dac vp
    lac i vp
    jda vfn
    dac vl
#ifdef RUNLOG
    dac rlb
#endif
    lac vlo
    dac vlu
    lac vhi
    dac vhu
#ifndef FIRSTHIT
    // The span takes in the held run, then the run is held in its place.
    lac hro
    dac vht
    lac hlo
    sub vlu
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp ve4
    lac hlo
    dac vlu
ve4,
    lac vhu
    sub hhi
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp ve5
    lac hhi
    dac vhu
ve5,
    lac vro
    dac hro
    lac vlo
    dac hlo
    lac vhi
    dac hhi
    law i VIDLE             // phit drops it after VIDLE idle turns more
    dac vq
    dzm vro
    lac vht
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME hro
    jmp ve7                 // none held on its track before it, so held, not judged
#else
    dzm vro
#endif
    lac vl
    sub vlu
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_NEGATIVE
    jmp ve1                 // left of the span
    lac vl
    sub vhu
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO_OR_NEGATIVE
    jmp ve2                 // right of it
#ifdef RUNLOG
    lac vl
    jda rlog
#endif
    jmp vex                 // within it, so kept
ve1,
    lac vlu
    jmp ve3
ve2,
    lac vhu
ve3,
#ifdef RUNLOG
    dac vl
    jda rlog
    lac vl
#endif
    add [vlv]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    dac i vp
    lio vr                  // to the converter, with the dynamic in force while a piece plays
    jsp i [dzv:3]
    lac vr
    jda vmk
    jmp vex
ve6,
    dzm hro
#ifndef FIRSTHIT
#ifdef RUNLOG
    jmp vex                 // past the log's mark (without the log, ve7 is vex)
#endif
ve7,
#ifdef RUNLOG
    law 077                 // the log's mark for a run held, not judged
    jda rlog
#endif
#endif
vex, jmp .

vl, 0                       // the level's point
vr, 0                       // the track
vp, 0                       // its word of ovol
vlu, 0                      // the span's first point
vhu, 0                      // and its last
#ifndef FIRSTHIT
vht, 0                      // the track held before, + 1
#endif
    endlocal

#ifdef RUNLOG
// rlog -- log a run vend judged into the ring rlg. Logs the menu's frame,
// the track, the run's first and last point, the level's point before,
// and after (AC). rln counts them; the ring is read from the console.
// Takes the point after in AC.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jda.
rlog, 0                     // AC, as jda stores it
    local rlx
    dap rlx
    lac rfc
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    lac rlt
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    lac vlo
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    lac vhi
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    lac rlb
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    lac rlog
    dac i rlp
    idx rlp
    idx rln
    lac rlp
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [rlg + RLOGW]
    jmp rlx
    law rlg                 // the ring wraps
    dac rlp
rlx, jmp .
    endlocal
#endif

// vmk -- set a converter's marker, at its level's point, and its readout.
// Takes the converter in AC, 0 to NCONV-1.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jda.
vmk, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local vkx, vkw, vkn
    dap vkx
    lac vmk
    add [vmw]
    dac vkw
    lac i vkw
    dac vkw                 // the marker's word
    lac vmk
    add [ovol]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    jda vfn
    dac vkn                 // the level's number, VN if it is none
    ral VSH                 // the point's x; VN (not a level) falls just right of the track
    add [VX0 | next(vector)]
    dac i vkw
    lac vmk
    add [vrw]
    dac vkw
    lac i vkw
    dac vkw                 // the readout's text word
    lac vkn
    add [vdb]
    dac vkn
    lac i vkn               // the level's text, ? for none
    dac i vkw
vkx, jmp .

vkw, 0                      // the marker's word, then the readout's
vkn, 0                      // the level's number, then its text's address
    endlocal

// vfn -- vlv's number for the level in AC, VN if it is not one.
// Takes the level in AC and returns the number in AC.
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jda.
vfn, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local vfx
    dap vfx
    lac vfn
    dac mt2
    law vlv
    dac mlt
    law VN
    dac mln
    lac mt2
    jda look
vfx, jmp .
    endlocal

// rdt -- READ TAPE. load's code reads every part, and an orchestra block,
// with atm set. Then nothing halts, rw ends the read at rte when no word
// comes, and an error in the tape ends it at rtx. Nothing in core changes
// until the first word.
// Has no arguments and does not return. It runs on into lds.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, from act.
rdt,
    crossBankjsp(drd:1, NOEEM) // the library's voices, for orb's numbers
    law 1
    dac atm
    law srd
    jda sts
    dzm got
    dzm rwn
    lac npart
    dac onp
    jmp lds

// rte -- no word came. Go back to the menu, with the parts already in
// core if none came at all. The status is TAPE READ, or the note rwn
// holds.
// Has no arguments and does not return. It ends at mnr.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, from rw.
rte,
    local re1, re2
    dzm atm
    lac got
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp re1
    lac onp
    dac npart
    law sno
    jmp re2
re1,
    lac rwn
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    law srr
re2,
    jda sts
    jmp mnr
    endlocal

// rtx -- an error in the tape ends READ TAPE. Its text goes on the status
// line, the parts read whole before it are kept, and the menu is shown
// again. The reader is not started, since the error came with the last
// word read.
// Takes the error's text in AC.
// Does not return. It ends at mnr.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Entered via jmp, from dacmusic.am1's loader.
rtx,
    dzm atm
    jda sts
    jmp mnr

// rw -- the next word from the reader, into IO. From the console (atm 0),
// an rpb, which waits as long as it takes. From READ TAPE, the reader is
// started without a transfer (bits 5 and 6 equal), status bit 1 says the
// word is in its buffer, and rrb takes it, as the D handbook gives it;
// meanwhile msv keeps the screen drawn, and no word in rto's polls
// (about 2 s, 12 s for the tape's first) ends the read at rte.
// That end leaves the read it started unfinished, and the reader keeps
// it. A tape mounted again completes it with the tape's first word. So
// a word already in the buffer is taken first, on either path; and
// while a read is started and not taken (rps), none is started again,
// and the console's path waits for that one's word instead of an rpb.
// Has no arguments.
// Returns the word in IO. On READ TAPE's time limit it does not return,
// but jumps to rte.
// Does not preserve AC.
// Called via jsp.
rw,
    local rw1, rw2, rw3, rw4, rw5, rw6, rw7, rw9, rwx, rto
    dap rwx
    cks
    ril 1s
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_IO_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO // skip unless status bit 1, so no word is in yet
    jmp rw6                 // a word is in already
rw5,
    lac atm
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp rw9
    lac got
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp rw1
    lac [0d120000]
    jmp rw2
rw1,
    lac [0d20000]
rw2,
    cma
    dac rto
    lac rps
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    rpb-i
    law 1
    dac rps
rw3,
    jsp msv
    cks
    ril 1s
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_IO_NEGATIVE // skip if status bit 1, the word is in
    jmp rw4
rw6,
    rrb
    dzm rps
    law 1
    dac got
    jmp rwx
rw4,
    isp rto
    jmp rw3
    jmp rte
rw9,
    lac rps
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp rw7
    rpb
    jmp rwx
rw7,
    cks                     // READ TAPE's read, still to come, as long as it takes
    ril 1s
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_IO_NEGATIVE
    jmp rw7
    jmp rw6
rwx, jmp .

rto, 0                      // polls left for this word
    endlocal

// msv -- keep the screen drawn while the program waits. A pen hit is
// passed over, a stopped display started again.
// Has no arguments and no return values.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jsp.
msv,
    local ms1, msx
    dap msx
    dsp
    jmp ms1
    drs
ms1,
    dss
    jmp msx
    lio [mlist]
    dla
msx, jmp .
    endlocal

// orb -- check the orchestra block's ct words, read to fp, and take them
// into per, orch, ostp, ovol and opl if every number is one the program
// has. A block of ORCHN words ends in the volumes; one of ORCHN0, the
// form without them, sets every volume to 0 dB; both have one stop a
// converter and set the converters' fixed places, 1 and 2 left, 3 and 4
// right. One of ORCHN2 is version 2 (Implementation.md, "Reading a
// tape"), whose lines have one to STOPS stops, packed from the first, and
// a place of the nine; it is taken only with no detune. One of ORCHN3 is
// version 3, version 2's words and then the room and the onset, each one
// of its field's (rmv and onv); every other form sets both to SETCFG, the
// configuration's.
// Whether stops sound together is vld's to say. A voice is one the
// drum's library has (ninst), or any of MAXV when the drum has none, and
// PLAY then says that it is missing.
// Takes ct, which is ORCHN, ORCHN0, ORCHN2 or ORCHN3.
// Returns 0 in AC if taken. Otherwise nothing is changed and AC is a
// converter (1 to NCONV) with a number out of range, a volume that is no
// level or a place not of the nine, or NCONV+1 for per, the version, the
// room or the onset.
// Does not preserve IO.
// Called via jsp.
orb,
    local ob1, ob2, ob3, ob4, ob5, ob6, ob7, ob9, obx, oc1, oc2, oc3, oc4, oc5, oc6, oc7, ocd
    dap obx
    lac ct
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [ORCHN2]
    jmp oc1
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [ORCHN3]
    jmp oc1
    // The volumes, the block's last NCONV words, or vzr's.
    law vzr
    dac mv
    lac ct
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [ORCHN]
    jmp ob3
    lac fp
    add [ORCHN - NCONV]
    dac mv
ob3,
    law NCONV               // per less 1, 0 to NCONV-1
    dac mlim
    lac fp
    dac mq
    lac i mq
    sub [1]
    jda rng
    jmp ob5
    lac fp
    dac mq
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
    dzm mc
ob1,
    idx mc
    idx mq
    law NCONV+1
    dac mlim
    lac i mq                // the part plus 1, 0 to NCONV
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    jsp vlim
    lac i mq                // the voice's number
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    law NOCT
    dac mlim
    lac i mq                // the octave's
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    isp mn
    jmp ob1
    lac mv
    dac mq
    dzm mc
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
ob6,
    idx mc
    lac i mq                // the volume
    jda vfn
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [VN]
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    isp mn
    jmp ob6
    // Every number good, so taken.
    lac fp
    dac mq
    lac i mq
    dac per
    law orch
    dac mp
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
ob2,
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    sub [1]                 // the part; 0 becomes -1, none
    dac i mp
    idx mp
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    dac i mp
    idx mp
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    add [octbl]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    dac i mp
    idx mp
    isp mn
    jmp ob2
    lac mv
    dac mq
    law ovol
    dac mp
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
ob4,
    lac i mq
    dac i mp
    idx mq
    idx mp
    isp mn
    jmp ob4
    law ostp                // one stop a converter
    dac mp
    law i 0d12              // NCONV * (STOPS - 1)
    dac mn
ob7,
    dzm i mp
    idx mp
    isp mn
    jmp ob7
    dzm opl                 // and the converters' fixed places
    dzm opl + 1
    law PLRIGHT
    dac opl + 2
    dac opl + 3
    jmp ocd
    // Versions 2 and 3. The version and per, then each line, then for
    // version 3 the room and the onset. A line is part + 1, octave,
    // volume, detune 0, a place of the nine, a voice + 1, then three
    // stops, each a voice + 1 after a voice, or 0. The version must be
    // the block's length's, 2, or 3 for its two words more.
oc1,
    lac ct
    sub [ORCHN2]
    sar 1s
    add [2]
    dac mt
    lac fp
    dac mq
    lac i mq
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME mt
    jmp ob5
    idx mq
    law NCONV               // per less 1, 0 to NCONV-1
    dac mlim
    lac i mq
    sub [1]
    jda rng
    jmp ob5
    dzm mc
oc2,
    idx mc
    idx mq
    law NCONV+1
    dac mlim
    lac i mq                // the part plus 1, 0 to NCONV
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    law NOCT
    dac mlim
    lac i mq                // the octave's number
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    lac i mq                // the volume
    jda vfn
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT [VN]
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    lac i mq                // the detune, which must be 0
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    law PLRIGHT + 1
    dac mlim
    lac i mq                // the place, one of the nine, 0 to PLRIGHT, 040 apart
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    lac i mq
    and [037]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    jmp ob9
    idx mq
    jsp vlim
    lac i mq                // the voice plus 1, the first stop
    sub [1]
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
    law i 3                 // STOPS - 1
    dac mn
oc4,
    lac i mq
    dac mt                  // the stop before
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp oc5
    lac mt
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp ob9                 // a stop after none
    lac i mq
    sub [1]
    jda rng
    jmp ob9
oc5,
    isp mn
    jmp oc4
    lac mc
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [NCONV]
    jmp oc2
    lac ct
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [ORCHN3]
    jmp oc7
    lac fp
    add [ORCHN2]
    dac mq
    lac [rmv:1]
    dac mlt
    law NRM
    dac mln
    lac i mq                // the room
    jda look
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT mln
    jmp ob5
    idx mq
    law onv
    dac mlt
    law NON
    dac mln
    lac i mq                // the onset
    jda look
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT mln
    jmp ob5
oc7,
    // Every number good, so taken.
    lac fp
    dac mq
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    dac per
    law orch
    dac mp
    law ovol
    dac mv
    law ostp
    dac ms
    law opl
    dac mo
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
oc3,
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    sub [1]                 // the part; 0 becomes -1, none
    dac i mp
    idx mp
    lac mq
    add [5]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    sub [1]                 // the voice
    dac i mp
    idx mp
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    add [octbl]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    dac i mp                // the octave's shift
    idx mp
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    dac i mv                // the volume
    idx mv
    lac mq
    add [2]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    dac i mo                // the place
    idx mo
    lac mq
    add [4]                 // the second stop
    dac mt
    law i 3                 // STOPS - 1
    dac mw
oc6,
    lac i mt
    dac i ms
    idx mt
    idx ms
    isp mw
    jmp oc6
    lac mq
    add [6]                 // to the line's last word
    dac mq
    isp mn
    jmp oc3
    lac ct
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [ORCHN3]
    jmp ocd
    idx mq                  // past the last line, the room, then the onset
    lac i mq
    dac oroom
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    dac onst
    cla
    jmp obx
ocd,
    lac [SETCFG]            // no room or onset, so the configuration's
    dac oroom
    dac onst
    cla
    jmp obx
ob5,
    law NCONV+1
    jmp obx
ob9,
    lac mc
obx, jmp .
    endlocal

// vlim -- set mlim to the voices orb takes, the library's (ninst), or
// MAXV when the drum has none.
// Has no arguments and no return values.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jsp.
vlim,
    local vmx
    dap vmx
    lac ninst
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    law MAXV
    dac mlim
vmx, jmp .
    endlocal

// rng -- skip if 0 <= AC < mlim.
// Takes the number in AC and the limit in mlim.
// Skips if the number is in range.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jda.
rng, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local rgx
    dap rgx
    lac rng
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO // skip if not negative
    jmp rgx
    sub mlim
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_NEGATIVE // skip if not below mlim
    idx rgx
rgx, jmp .
    endlocal

// fill -- set the screen's changing words from the program's state, and
// give the device the room and the onset the screen shows.
// Has no arguments and no return values.
// Does not preserve AC or IO.
// Called via jsp.
fill,
    local fl0, fl1, fl2, fl3, fl4, fl5, fl6, fl7, fl8, fl9, fla, flb, flc, fld, flx, mr
    dap flx
    lac npart
    jda num
    dac mnp
    lac per
    jda num
    dac mpr
    // The movements, npart / per, rounded up.
    dzm mt
    lac per
    sma sza i               // skip if per is above 0; else no movements
    jmp fl3
fl0,
    lac npart
    dac mr
fl1,
    lac mr
    sma sza i               // skip if parts are left
    jmp fl3
fl2,
    sub per
    dac mr
    idx mt
    jmp fl1
fl3,
    lac mt
    jda num
    dac mmv
    // Each converter's part, instrument and octave.
    law orch
    dac mq
    law mfw
    dac mp
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
fl4,
    law NCONV               // pnm's texts, one a part
    dac mlim
    lac i mq
    jda rng
    jmp fl5
    lac i mq
    add [pnm]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    jmp fl7
fl5,
    lac i mq
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO // skip if not negative, past the last part
    jmp fl6
    law squ
    jmp fl7
fl6,
    law snn
fl7,
    jda fput
    idx mq
    lac ninst               // the voice's name in the directory, if it has the voice
    dac mlim
    lac i mq
    jda rng
    jmp fl8
    lac i mq
    ral 3s                  // ENTRY (8) words a voice
    add [dir:1 + EBASE]
    jmp fl9
fl8,
    law squ
fl9,
    jda fput
    idx mq
    lac i mq
    jda ofn
    add [onam]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    jda fput
    idx mq
    isp mn
    jmp fl4
    // Each instrument's further stops, counted, +1 to +3 after its name,
    // or nothing.
    law ostp
    dac mq
    law mcf
    dac mp
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
flb,
    law stc
    dac mt
    law i 3                 // STOPS - 1
    dac mw
flc,
    lac i mq
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_ZERO
    idx mt
    idx mq
    isp mw
    jmp flc
    lac i mt
    jda fput
    isp mn
    jmp flb
    // Each converter's place, by its name, or ? if it is not one of plv's.
    law opl
    dac mq
    law mlw
    dac mp
    law i NCONV
    dac mn
    lac [plv:3]
    dac mlt
    law NPL
    dac mln
fld,
    lac i mq
    jda look
    add [pnt:3]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    jda fput
    idx mq
    isp mn
    jmp fld
    // The room and the onset, by their names, or ? if not of the lists';
    // the device is given both, so an audition sounds in them.
    lac [rmv:1]
    dac mlt
    law NRM
    dac mln
    lac oroom
    jda look
    add [rmt:3]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    ior [SAVEC]
    dac mrf
    law onv
    dac mlt
    law NON
    dac mln
    lac onst
    jda look
    add [ont:3]
    dac mt
    lac i mt
    ior [SAVEC]
    dac mnf
    lio oroom
    dye
    lio onst
    dyo
    // Each converter's marker.
    dzm mr
fla,
    lac mr
    jda vmk
    idx mr
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_SAME [NCONV]
    jmp fla
flx, jmp .

mr, 0                       // the parts not yet in a movement; a converter, for its marker
    endlocal

// fput -- make the field word mp names (mp walks mfw) a save to the text
// at AC; mp moves on.
// Takes the text's address in AC.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jda.
fput, 0                     // AC, as jda stores it
    local fpx, mt3, mt4
    dap fpx
    lac fput
    ior [SAVEC]
    dac mt3
    lac i mp
    dac mt4
    lac mt3
    dac i mt4
    idx mp
fpx, jmp .

mt3, 0                      // the save
mt4, 0                      // the field word
    endlocal

// sts -- show the text at AC on the status line.
// Takes the text's address in AC.
// No return value.
// Does not preserve AC; preserves IO.
// Called via jda.
sts, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local ssx
    dap ssx
    lac sts
    ior [SAVEC]
    dac mstl
ssx, jmp .
    endlocal

// num -- AC (0-99) as one word of 340 text, its digits, then the end.
// Takes the number in AC and returns the word in AC.
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jda.
num, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local nm1, nm2, nm3, nmx, mnm, mtn
    dap nmx
    lac num
    dac mnm
    dzm mtn
nm1,
    lac mnm
    sub [0d10]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE // skip if below ten
    jmp nm3
    lac mtn
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NOT_ZERO
    jmp nm2
    add [060]               // two digits, tens, units, the end
    ral 6s
    add mnm
    add [060]
    ral 6s
    add [037]
    jmp nmx
nm2,
    lac mnm                 // one digit, the end
    add [060]
    ral 6s
    add [037]
    ral 6s
    jmp nmx
nm3,
    dac mnm
    idx mtn
    jmp nm1
nmx, jmp .

mnm, 0                      // the number, its tens taken off
mtn, 0                      // its tens
    endlocal

// fnd -- the opener or button whose band and column hold drc's point.
// Takes drc's word in IO.
// Returns the number in AC, 0 to NTGT-1, or NTGT if none holds it (a
// track's point, or a gap's).
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jsp.
fnd,
    local fd1, fd2, fd3, fd4, fd5, fd6, fd7, fd8, fb1, fb2, fb3, fb4, fdn, fdx, fx, fy, fr
    dap fdx
    dio mt2
    lac mt2
    and [0777]
    ral 1s
    dac fy
    lac mt2
    rar 9s
    and [0777]
    ral 1s
    dac fx
    lac fy
    sub [FPB]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp fd1                 // the parts a movement
    lac fy
    sub [FRT]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp fdn                 // above the rows
    lac fy
    sub [FRB]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd3                 // below them
    // A row, 0 to NCONV-1 from the top.
    lac [FRT]
    sub fy
    dac mt
    dzm fr
fd2,
    lac mt
    sub [FRP]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd4
    dac mt
    idx fr
    jmp fd2
    // Its column.
fd4,
    lac fx
    sub [FXV]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd8                 // the place's
    sub [FXP - FXV]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd5                 // the part's
    sub [FXI - FXP]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd6                 // the instrument's
    sub [FXO - FXI]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fd7                 // the octave's
    jmp fdn
fd5,
    lac fr
    jmp fdx
fd6,
    lac fr
    add [NCONV]
    jmp fdx
fd7,
    lac fr
    add [2 * NCONV]
    jmp fdx
fd8,
    lac fr
    add [0d16]
    jmp fdx
    // The buttons.
fd3,
    lac fy
    sub [FBT]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_NEGATIVE
    jmp fdn
    lac fy
    sub [FBB]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fdn
    lac fx
    sub [FXR]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fb1
    sub [FXL - FXR]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fb2
    sub [FXU - FXL]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fb3
    sub [FXM - FXU]
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_AC_POSITIVE_OR_ZERO
    jmp fb4
    law 0d24                // the onset's
    jmp fdx
fb4,
    law 0d20                // the room's
    jmp fdx
fdn,
    law NTGT
    jmp fdx
fd1,
    law 0d12
    jmp fdx
fb1,
    law 0d13
    jmp fdx
fb2,
    law 0d14
    jmp fdx
fb3,
    law 0d15
fdx, jmp .

fx, 0                       // the point's x
fy, 0                       // and its y
fr, 0                       // its row
    endlocal

// ofn -- octbl's number for the shift in AC, NOCT if it is not there.
// Takes the shift in AC and returns the number in AC.
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jda.
ofn, 0                      // AC, as jda stores it
    local ofx
    dap ofx
    lac ofn
    dac mt2
    law octbl
    dac mlt
    law NOCT
    dac mln
    lac mt2
    jda look
ofx, jmp .
    endlocal

// look -- the index of AC in the table at mlt, mln words long.
// Takes the value in AC, the table in mlt and its length in mln.
// Returns the index in AC, or mln if the value is not there.
// IO is preserved.
// Called via jda.
look, 0                     // AC, as jda stores it
    local lk1, lk2, lkx, mlv, mlk, mlp
    dap lkx
    lac look
    dac mlv
    dzm mlk
lk1,
    lac mlk
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT mln
    jmp lkx
    add mlt
    dac mlp
    lac i mlp
    SKIP_NEXT_IF_DIFFERENT mlv
    jmp lk2
    idx mlk
    jmp lk1
lk2,
    lac mlk
lkx, jmp .

mlv, 0                      // the value
mlk, 0                      // the index
mlp, 0                      // its word
    endlocal

// The screen.

// The display list, the gate, then the texts and the sliders both screens
// show, then msw. Its rows, and so the openers in a column and the
// tracks, are 60 points apart, the openers in a row at least 30 apart
// with the longest name the directory holds (17 letters, 238 units), and
// a track's first point 34 from the octave's opener. So the pen's reach
// at PENAP (20) never takes two openers at once, nor an opener and a
// track, nor two tracks.
mlist,
    scale(1) intensity(5) lpoff next(subroutine)
mgt, jump mbody next(parameter) // or menus.ac's open list
mbody,
    AT(0d60, 0d900)
    type340 "\UDAC MUSIC"
    AT(0d240, 0d900)
mnp, 0                      // the parts read
    next(character)
    type340 " PARTS"
    AT(0d380, 0d900)
mmv, 0                      // the movements
    next(character)
    type340 " MOVEMENTS"
mo13, OPN(0d636, 0d900, character)
    type340 "PARTS A MOVEMENT "
    next(character)
mpr, 0                      // per

mo14, OPN(0d60, 0d780, character)
    type340 "1 "
    next(subroutine)
mlf1, SAVEC | squ                  // its place
mo1, OPN(0d216, 0d780, character)
    type340 "PART "
    next(subroutine)
mpf1, SAVEC | squ
mo5, OPN(0d386, 0d780, subroutine)
mif1, SAVEC | squ
    next(subroutine)
mic1, SAVEC | sbl                  // its further stops' count (fill)
mo9, OPN(0d656, 0d780, subroutine)
mof1, SAVEC | squ

mo15, OPN(0d60, 0d720, character)
    type340 "2 "
    next(subroutine)
mlf2, SAVEC | squ                  // its place
mo2, OPN(0d216, 0d720, character)
    type340 "PART "
    next(subroutine)
mpf2, SAVEC | squ
mo6, OPN(0d386, 0d720, subroutine)
mif2, SAVEC | squ
    next(subroutine)
mic2, SAVEC | sbl                  // its further stops' count (fill)
mo10, OPN(0d656, 0d720, subroutine)
mof2, SAVEC | squ

mo16, OPN(0d60, 0d660, character)
    type340 "3 "
    next(subroutine)
mlf3, SAVEC | squ                  // its place
mo3, OPN(0d216, 0d660, character)
    type340 "PART "
    next(subroutine)
mpf3, SAVEC | squ
mo7, OPN(0d386, 0d660, subroutine)
mif3, SAVEC | squ
    next(subroutine)
mic3, SAVEC | sbl                  // its further stops' count (fill)
mo11, OPN(0d656, 0d660, subroutine)
mof3, SAVEC | squ

mo17, OPN(0d60, 0d600, character)
    type340 "4 "
    next(subroutine)
mlf4, SAVEC | squ                  // its place
mo4, OPN(0d216, 0d600, character)
    type340 "PART "
    next(subroutine)
mpf4, SAVEC | squ
mo8, OPN(0d386, 0d600, subroutine)
mif4, SAVEC | squ
    next(subroutine)
mic4, SAVEC | sbl                  // its further stops' count (fill)
mo12, OPN(0d656, 0d600, subroutine)
mof4, SAVEC | squ

    // The sliders, at the rows' height; vmk patches the markers' x and
    // the readouts' texts.
    TRACK(0d786)
mk1, x(VX0 + 0d15 * VDX) next(vector)
    MARK
    READOUT(0d786)
md1, RDW(CSP, CSP, CD(0))
    RDE
    TRACK(0d726)
mk2, x(VX0 + 0d15 * VDX) next(vector)
    MARK
    READOUT(0d726)
md2, RDW(CSP, CSP, CD(0))
    RDE
    TRACK(0d666)
mk3, x(VX0 + 0d15 * VDX) next(vector)
    MARK
    READOUT(0d666)
md3, RDW(CSP, CSP, CD(0))
    RDE
    TRACK(0d606)
mk4, x(VX0 + 0d15 * VDX) next(vector)
    MARK
    READOUT(0d606)
md4, RDW(CSP, CSP, CD(0))
    RDE
    intensity(5) next(subroutine)
msw, jump mtl next(parameter) // mswm or mswp

// The menu's tail, the buttons, the room's and the onset's fields, and
// the status line, then a stop. The play tail has no room or onset, as
// neither can change while the piece plays.
mtl,
    OPN(0d60, 0d480, character)
    type340 "READ TAPE"
    OPN(0d260, 0d480, character)
    type340 "PLAY"
    OPN(0d400, 0d480, character)
    type340 "PUNCH"
    OPN(0d560, 0d480, character)
    type340 "ROOM "
    next(subroutine)
mrf, SAVEC | squ            // the room's field
    OPN(0d820, 0d480, character)
    type340 "ONSET "
    next(subroutine)
mnf, SAVEC | squ            // the onset's field
    ATQ(0d60, 0d420)
mstl, SAVEC | sbl            // the status line
    lpoff halt

// The play tail, PLAYING and STOP beside it, then the list again. STOP's
// point is about 57 units from the nearest of PLAY's, beyond the pen's
// reach, so a pen still there does not stop the piece it started, nor a
// pen left on STOP start the next. Six vector continues, about 1.5 ms
// each, with the sliders' 3.2 ms, pace the screen at about 60 frames a
// second, fast enough not to flicker.
mpt,
    AT(0d60, 0d420)
    type340 "PLAYING"
    TGT(0d240, 0d426)
    AT(0d256, 0d420)
    type340 "STOP"
    scale(0) next(point)
    y(0) next(point)
    x(0) next(vcontinue)
    right deltax(1)
    WAIT; WAIT; WAIT; WAIT; WAIT
    next(subroutine)
    jump mlist next(parameter)

// msw's two words.
mswm, jump mtl next(parameter)
mswp, jump mpt next(parameter)

// The texts the fields and the status line show.
pnm, pn1; pn2; pn3; pn4     // the parts' numbers, and the converters' in a list's header
pn1, type340 "1"
pn2, type340 "2"
pn3, type340 "3"
pn4, type340 "4"
snn, type340 "NONE"
squ, type340 "?"
// The room's and the onset's names (rmt and ont, in bank 3, in punch.ac),
// and their lists' headers. The room's NONE is snn.
txCfg, type340 "CONFIG"
txHall, type340 "HALL"
txBusch, type340 "BUSCH HALL"
txVoices, type340 "VOICES"
txOff, type340 "OFF"
txOn2, type340 "2 MS"
txOn4, type340 "4 MS"
txOn6, type340 "6 MS"
txOn8, type340 "8 MS"
txOn12, type340 "12 MS"
txOn16, type340 "16 MS"
txRoom, type340 "ROOM"
txOnset, type340 "ONSET"
// The onset's field, its values in 1/8 ms (dyo), SETCFG for the
// configuration's. The room's values (rmv) are in bank 1 (menus.ac), and
// both fields' names, with ? last for a value not among them (fill), are
// in bank 3 (punch.ac), to save room in bank 0. Each is reached through
// its full address.
onv, SETCFG; 0; 020; 040; 060; 0100; 0140; 0200
// Each list's five words for lsto (menus.ac). They are where OK puts its
// value, its header, its rows' names and values, and their count,
// negative.
rlists,
    oroom; SAVEC | txRoom; rmt:3; rmv:1; 0777777 - NRM
    onst; SAVEC | txOnset; ont:3; onv; 0777777 - NON
// The octaves, their shifts, executed on a step (orch's third word),
// then their texts; an octave's place in octbl is its number in the
// orchestra block. The sixth text is for a shift not in octbl.
octbl, nop; sar 1s; ral 1s; sar 2s; ral 2s
onam, on8; on16; on4; on32; on2; squ
on8, type340 "8 FT"
on16, type340 "16 FT"
on4, type340 "4 FT"
on32, type340 "32 FT"
on2, type340 "2 FT"
sbl, type340 " "
srd, type340 "READING TAPE"
srr, type340 "TAPE READ"
sno, type340 "NO TAPE"
spu, type340 "PUNCHING TAPE"
spd, type340 "TAPE PUNCHED"
sst, type340 "STOPPED"
sbc, type340 "TAPE ERROR BAD COUNT"
stm, type340 "TAPE ERROR TOO MANY PARTS"
stl, type340 "TAPE ERROR TAPE TOO LARGE"
sck, type340 "TAPE READ CHECKSUM ERROR"
sor, type340 "TAPE READ ORCHESTRA REFUSED"
sld, type340 "LOADING VOICES"
snv, type340 "NO VOICES ON THE DRUM"
snl, type340 "VOICE NOT IN THE LIBRARY"
sbg, type340 "VOICES TOO LARGE"
// VOICE n DAMAGED, RELOAD THE DRUM. "VOI" and "CE " as 340 text, the
// number's word (rsn puts it in sdn), then the rest.
sdm, 261711; 030540
sdn, 0
    type340 "DAMAGED, RELOAD THE DRUM"
ssm, type340 "STOPS DO NOT MATCH"
stc, sbl; stc1; stc2; stc3   // an instrument's further stops, by their count
stc1, type340 "+1"
stc2, type340 "+2"
stc3, type340 "+3"
svt, snv; snl; sdm; sbg; ssm; sft:1 // vld's AC 1-6

// The sliders' tables. The levels, left to right, in 1/8 dB of
// attenuation. A finer step changes VSTEP, VN, this table and the tracks'
// points, nothing else.
vlv,
    0d15 * VSTEP; 0d14 * VSTEP; 0d13 * VSTEP; 0d12 * VSTEP
    0d11 * VSTEP; 0d10 * VSTEP; 0d9 * VSTEP; 0d8 * VSTEP
    0d7 * VSTEP; 0d6 * VSTEP; 0d5 * VSTEP; 0d4 * VSTEP
    0d3 * VSTEP; 0d2 * VSTEP; 0d1 * VSTEP; 0
vty, 0d786 >> 1; 0d726 >> 1; 0d666 >> 1; 0d606 >> 1 // each track's y, as drc gives it
vmw, mk1; mk2; mk3; mk4     // each marker's word
vrw, md1; md2; md3; md4     // each readout's text word
vzr, 0; 0; 0; 0             // the volumes for a block without them, 0 dB
// The readouts' texts, by vlv's number, -45 dB to 0, then a level that
// is none of them. BADREADOUT builds show -33 at -30, a deliberate
// fault.
vdb,
    RDW(CMI, CD(4), CD(5)); RDW(CMI, CD(4), CD(2)); RDW(CMI, CD(3), CD(0d9))
    RDW(CMI, CD(3), CD(6)); RDW(CMI, CD(3), CD(3))
#ifdef BADREADOUT
    RDW(CMI, CD(3), CD(3))
#else
    RDW(CMI, CD(3), CD(0))
#endif
    RDW(CMI, CD(2), CD(7)); RDW(CMI, CD(2), CD(4)); RDW(CMI, CD(2), CD(1))
    RDW(CMI, CD(1), CD(0d8)); RDW(CMI, CD(1), CD(5)); RDW(CMI, CD(1), CD(2))
    RDW(CSP, CMI, CD(0d9)); RDW(CSP, CMI, CD(6)); RDW(CSP, CMI, CD(3))
    RDW(CSP, CSP, CD(0))
    RDW(CSP, CSP, CQU)

// The menu's words.

atm, 0                      // reading from the menu, so no halts, errors on the status line
got, 0                      // READ TAPE has had a word
onp, 0                      // the parts in core before it
rwn, 0                      // its note for the end, sck or sor, 0 if none
rps, 0                      // a read started and its word not taken; 0 at each start (menu, load)
mnu, 0                      // the piece was started from the menu
hpl, 0                      // set from the console to halt at lpl before the piece, lpe after it
hit, 0                      // this frame's first hit, fnd's number + 1, or 1 with a list open
arm, 0                      // a hit will count
qt, 0                       // passes left until the pen counts as away
pap, 0                      // the pen's aperture, PENAP or a list's
lon, 0                      // a list is open (menus.ac)
lhw, 0                      // its frame's first hit, drc's word
ltg, 0                      // the opener act opens, fnd's number
mc, 0                       // a converter, 0 to NCONV-1, or orb's 1 to NCONV
mq, 0                       // the word read next, orch's or a block's
mp, 0                       // the next word, of orch or of mfw
mo, 0                       // orb's next word of opl
mt, 0                       // scratch
mw, 0                       // a count
mt2, 0                      // the value vhit, vfn and ofn give look; fnd's drc word
mn, 0                       // a count
ms, 0                       // orb's next word of ostp
mpn, 0                      // mpo's count
mlim, 0                     // rng's limit
mlt, 0                      // look's table
mln, 0                      // and its words
mv, 0                       // orb's volumes, the block's or vzr
vro, 0                      // a run of hits on a track, the track + 1, 0 if none
vlo, 0                      // its first point, 0 to VN-1
vhi, 0                      // its last
vq, 0                       // phit's turns left until the run ends, or the held run is dropped
hro, 0                      // the run vend holds, the track + 1, 0 if none
hlo, 0                      // its first point
hhi, 0                      // its last
#ifdef RUNLOG
rlp, 0                      // the ring's next word
rln, 0                      // the runs logged since the start
rfc, 0                      // the menu's frames since the start
rlt, 0                      // vend's track, for rlog
rlb, 0                      // vend's point before, for rlog
rlg,                        // the ring
    table RLOGW
#endif
